WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.240
Now, I make my living talking to people.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.750
Nobel Prize winners, truck drivers, billionaires,

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.630
kindergarten teachers, heads of state, plumbers.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:10.799
I talk to people that I like.

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:12.640
I talk to people that I don't like.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.610
I talk to some people that I disagree with
deeply on a personal level.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.000
But I still have a great conversation with
them.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.420
So I have 10 basic rules.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.730
I'm going to walk you through all of them,
but honestly,

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.810
if you just choose one of them and master
it,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.960
you'll already enjoy better conversations.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.730
Number one: Don't multitask.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.750
And I don't mean just set down your cell phone
or your tablet

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.750
or your car keys or whatever is in your hand.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.950
I mean be present.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.250
Be in that moment.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.770
Number two: Don't pontificate.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.710
If you want to state your opinion without
any opportunity

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.870
for response or argument or pushback or growth,

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.600
write a blog.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.940
Number three: Use open-ended questions.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.000
Start your questions with who, what, where,
when, why or how.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.640
If I ask you, "Were you terrified?"

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.300
you're going to respond to the most powerful
word

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.490
in that sentence, which is "terrified,"

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:06.000
and the answer is, "Yes, I was," or "No, I
wasn't."

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.650
Try asking them things like, "What was that
like?"

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.360
"How did that feel?"

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.720
Because then they might have to stop for a
moment

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.920
and think about it,

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.970
and you're going to get a much more interesting
response.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.870
Number four: Go with the flow.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.570
That means thoughts will come into your mind

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:26.910
and you need to let them go out of your mind.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:30.690
Number five: If you don't know, say that you
don't know.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.560
Err on the side of caution.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.960
Talk should not be cheap.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.620
Number six: Don't equate your experience with
theirs.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.620
It's not the same.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.840
It is never the same.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.350
All experiences are individual.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.280
And, more importantly, it is not about you.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.580
Conversations are not a promotional opportunity.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.659
Number seven: Try not to repeat yourself.

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:59.140
It's condescending, and it's really boring,
and we tend to do it a lot.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.140
Number eight: Stay out of the weeds.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:07.850
Frankly, people don't care about the years,
the names, the dates,

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.400
all those details that you're struggling to
come up with in your mind.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.400
They don t care.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.090
What they care about is you.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.180
Number nine: This is not the last one,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.170
but it is the most important one.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.170
Listen.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.340
Buddha said, and I'm paraphrasing,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.950
"If your mouth is open, you're not learning."

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.870
It takes effort and energy to actually pay
attention to someone,

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.550
but if you can't do that, you're not in a
conversation.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.450
You're just two people shouting out barely
related sentences

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.510
in the same place.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.890
One more rule, number 10, and it's this one:

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:40.890
Be brief.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:45.552
All of this boils down to the same basic concept,
and it is this one: 

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.430
Be interested in other people.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.310
I keep my mouth shut as often as I possibly
can,

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:55.490
I keep my mind open, and I'm always prepared
to be amazed,

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:58.180
and I'm never disappointed.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.970
You do the same thing.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:05.080
Go out, talk to people, listen to people,
and most importantly,

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.710
be prepared to be amazed.

